rs/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441887117","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/445#issuecomment-441887117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/445","id":441887117,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTg4NzExNw==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-09-05T13:42:13Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T03:22:58Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nfor future usage requests, please use the mailing list at https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/sqlalchemy-alembic.\n\nThe revision command can be intercepted using the hook described at http://alembic.zzzcomputing.com/en/latest/api/autogenerate.html#customizing-revision-generation.\n\nFirst make sure you specify `revision_environment = True` in your config, so that even a revision command that does not use `--autogenerate` will trigger the hook:\n\n```\n#!\n\n\n# set to 'true' to run the environment during\n# the 'revision' command, regardless of autogenerate\n# revision_environment = false\nrevision_environment = true\n\n```\n\n\nthen put your assertions in a custom process_revision_directives function in env.py:\n\n```\n#!\n\n\ndef process_revision_directives(context, revision, directives):\n    directive = directives[0]\n    if not directive.message:\n        raise ValueError(\"message is required\")\n    if not re.search(r'#\\d{6}', directive.message):\n        raise ValueError(\"Bug #dddddd is required\")\n\n```\n\nlink to migration operation:\n\n\n```\n#!\n\ndef run_migrations_online():\n   # ...\n    with connectable.connect() as connection:\n        context.configure(\n            connection=connection,\n            target_metadata=target_metadata,\n            process_revision_directives=process_revision_directives\n        )\n\n        with context.begin_transaction():\n            context.run_migrations()\n\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441887117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event